experience.description:
•	Working on Financial Accounting & Advisory work, including Accounting Policies & Procedures work on select assignments;

•	Responsible for identifying and building new training opportunities for the EY Corporate Training entity;

•	Successfully conducted several corporate and open-house trainings;

•	Coordinated all training activities with the EMEIA Training Team e.g. Creating a common share point for all training activities, submission of routine monthly training updates to the region, conducting annual training meetings for the EMEIA team within the MENA region, arranging one-on-one calls with the  EMEIA team on a monthly basis; 

•	Successfully converting existing Audit relationships into training opportunities. This was achieved by weekly pursuits and discussions with Audit Managers / Partners and tapping key Audit engagements for training possibilities

•	Successfully managed and received invaluable hands-on experience in routine administrative issues e.g. Writing up proposals, making budgets, liaising with clients and follow-ups, raising internal training entries on the Interaction system etc.

•	Successfully liaised with the management of key British Universities in order to tap into the possibilities of partnering into joint products – executive education and Masters in International Finance;

•	One of the key players to open training business into the Iranian market; successfully conducted a breakthrough IFRS Seminar in Tehran in April 2017. 

•	In addition to training activities, assisted management with other Financial Advisory related work.
